1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,660
Every billionaire's fortune, split eight billion ways. Here's your check.

2
00:00:05,460 --> 00:00:08,860
Forbes counted three thousand four hundred twenty-eight billionaires in March.

3
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:11,760
Together, they're worth twenty point one trillion dollars.

4
00:00:12,680 --> 00:00:14,660
A trillion is a thousand billions.

5
00:00:15,080 --> 00:00:17,420
But most of it is company shares, not cash.

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:20,420
Now pretend it's all cash, handed out once.

7
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:22,660
Hit like if you already picked what you'd buy.

8
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:26,040
Then split it between about eight point two billion people.

9
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:29,120
Every baby and every grandma gets the same check.

10
00:00:29,120 --> 00:00:31,940
And that check is about two thousand four hundred fifty dollars.

11
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:35,660
But that's once. Not per month, not per year.

12
00:00:36,280 --> 00:00:38,580
Now send this to the friend who says we'd all be millionaires.

13
00:00:39,400 --> 00:00:42,720
Spread over one year, that's six dollars and seventy cents a day.

14
00:00:43,080 --> 00:00:45,280
That's roughly a sandwich a day, then it's gone.

15
00:00:45,740 --> 00:00:49,460
The twist? In one year, that list grew about four trillion dollars.

16
00:00:50,260 --> 00:00:53,140
That growth alone is four hundred eighty-eight dollars each.

17
00:00:53,700 --> 00:00:55,640
Follow if your brain just did a double take.

18
00:00:55,640 --> 00:00:59,000
The average billionaire? Almost five point nine billion dollars.

19
00:00:59,840 --> 00:01:02,640
That's the same as two point four million people's checks.

20
00:01:03,140 --> 00:01:05,800
The pile is huge, but so is eight billion.

21
00:01:06,340 --> 00:01:09,280
Would a two thousand four hundred fifty dollar check change your year?

